    <h2 class="lesson-heading">Checklist <SourceBadge source="course" /></h2>

    <LessonChecklist
      title="Before chaining a task:"
      items={[
        '<strong>List the sub-tasks</strong> — each with one clear goal',
        '<strong>Give each sub-task its own prompt</strong> — don’t pack several goals into one',
        '<strong>Pass outputs forward explicitly</strong> — in code, each call only knows what you send it',
        '<strong>Check where a step needs real data</strong> — that step needs a tool, not just a prompt',
        '<strong>Refine steps individually</strong> — improve the weakest link, not the whole chain',
        '<strong>Pick workflow or agent</strong> — fixed steps known upfront → hard-coded chain; steps depend on findings → agent',
        '<strong>Make branch decisions parseable</strong> — ask for Yes/No (or a fixed label) when code branches on an LLM answer',
        '<strong>Plan a check after each step</strong> — an early error dominoes through the rest',
        '<strong>Cover format, content, and logic</strong> — structure first, then substance, then sense',
        '<strong>Choose the failure policy per step</strong> — halt for sensitive data, retry for random slips, retry with reasons for systematic ones',
        '<strong>Return the reasons a check failed</strong> — they become the feedback in the retry prompt',
        '<strong>Cap the retries</strong> — a feedback loop needs a maximum, just like the ReAct loop',
        '<strong>Fence inserted outputs</strong> — mark where the previous step’s output starts and ends in the next prompt',
        '<strong>Strip Markdown fences before parsing code</strong> — or valid code fails the syntax gate',
      ]}
    />

